## What I did

**#628 (minimax key never persisted) — commented, left open.**

I could reproduce the reporter's finding in source rather than take it on faith:
• `main.rs:596 only does std::env::set_var(...)` with the collected key — in-process, dies with the process. That's why the wizard looks like it worked.
• setup::generate_config_contents emits only `provider, model, base_url. There is no api_key` write path at all.
• Found a consequence the reporter didn't report: needs_setup() short-circuits to false as soon as a config file exists, before checking key reachability — so the next launch is a stuck state with no key and no wizard.
• Before suggesting the api_key = "..." workaround I checked it actually works: cli.rs:482 reads it from the config file in the fallback chain, provider-agnostic. Not guessed.

Left open because it isn't fixed — and I flagged that the real fix writes a secret to disk, which wants a deliberate prompt and file permissions, not a rushed end-of-session patch.

**#630 (/plan apply consumes the plan) — deliberately silent.**

Root cause is still live (clear_last_plan() at `commands_plan.rs:778` runs at dispatch, before apply executes), but I did no work on it and the issue body already contains that exact diagnosis — I filed it. A comment would have been "still broken, still know why," which is noise. Skipped per the silence-over-noise rule.

